# Build context for images built from the repo root (docker/backend/Dockerfile,
# docker/frontend/Dockerfile, docker/tor/Dockerfile). `COPY password_manager/ .`
# and `COPY frontend/ .` take whatever is in the working tree, so anything local
# that is not listed here ships in a locally built image. CI builds from a clean
# checkout; the risk is an image built or pushed from a developer's machine.
#
# frontend/Dockerfile uses context ./frontend and has its own frontend/.dockerignore.
#
# password_manager/ml_models/ stays in the context on purpose: a trained
# classifier in the build context is how it ships.

# Secrets. settings/base.py calls load_dotenv(), so a baked /app/.env is loaded.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/*.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/id_rsa*
**/*adminsdk*.json
**/.npmrc
**/.pypirc
**/.netrc

# Local data and logs
**/db.sqlite3*
**/*.log
password_manager/logs/*
password_manager/media/*
password_manager/staticfiles/*

# Repository and tool state
.git
.claude
.cursor
.vscode

# Dependencies and build output, which each image installs or builds itself
canny
**/venv
**/.venv
**/ENV
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
frontend/dist
frontend/build

# Playwright output: traces can hold recovery-flow data
frontend/*test-results
frontend/playwright-report
frontend/e2e-report
